{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1154024-help-me-understand-mask-dirge","id":1154024,"title":"Help me understand Mask & Dirge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-29T17:42:28-07:00","id":1154024,"title":"Help me understand Mask & Dirge","content":"So re-reading the VTR Core, i am looking at Mask and Dirgue and i simply dont get how the work in relation with their archetypes.<br /> <br /> So page 84 says <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR Core Mask;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any time a vampire overcomes a small hurdle in defense of her Mask, she gains a point of Willpower. When committing atrocious or existentially risky acts in defense of her Mask, she regains all her spent Willpower points.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR Core Dirge;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any time a vampire withdraws from his outside life in defense of his truer self, he gains a point of Willpower. When committing terrible, damning acts in defense of his personal identity, he regains all his spent Willpower points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems simple enough, one is the face you show to the humans and the other is your true face. So say for example my character Mask is Child and his Dirge is Monster. The when she takes pain in appear as a harmless child by, let say for example, letting a human hit her. The she would gain a WP point for her Mask. <br /> <br /> Same with her dirge, if she once in a while disappears to hunt a kill someone very slowly and thus raising question about her whereabouts she would regain a WP point for her dirge.<br /> <br /> However the archetypes confuse me because their example acts dont relate to protecting the mask or sacrificing the her human facade for the Dirge. They just actions that relate to the archetype.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR Core Authoritarian;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Single Willpower:</b> Shut down an inferior trying to rise to your level of power.<br /> <br /> <b>All Willpower:</b> Commit a widespread hit against a rival\u2019s mortal connections.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does that relate to Dirge or Mask? How thats related to committing atrocious acts in defense of being authoritarian? And/or commiting acts in defense of personal identity?<br /> <br /> I understand that mask and dirge are about the defending one face over the other but then the archetypes are just action that give WP regardless if they protect their identity or no.<br /> <br /> <br /> Any help would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T18:35:29-07:00","id":1154034,"title":"","content":"I consider the examples given to be posable ways to regain willpower from your Mask/Dirge not the only way, I also never require more than being strongly guided by your Mask/Dirge to gain willpower, finally I prefer to use Mask as that part of yourself you present to others (not just humans) and Dirge to be a more inner self type for example a Guru Mask Chalenger Dirge would help people because he gets to test himself against their problems whereas a Chalenger Mask Guru Dirge would get in your face and antagonise you to guide you towards a way to solve your problems.<br /> Hope that was some help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-29T19:33:26-07:00","id":1154041,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I understand where the problem is.<br /> <br /> Authoritarian reads:<br /> <br /> &quot;An authoritarian must be on top. She prides herself not in<br /> competition, but in control. She must assert her superiority and<br /> dominance whenever possible.&quot;<br /> <br /> Those sample actions fit perfectly well within the description of the Authoritarian Mask/Dirge.<br /> <br /> If it's a Mask, they're acting the control-freak to hide their weaknesses and appear strong. If it's a Dirge, they're doing it because they simply are a control-freak. Either way, the actions are the same; it's the motives that differ. &quot;Defense&quot; is mostly poetic language here; mostly it's just acting in line with your Mask/Dirge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T10:08:03-07:00","id":1154156,"title":"","content":"Take a look at page 81/82 in the rulebook. There, the Mask and Dirge are defined:<br /> <br /> &quot;Kindred wear Masks in public. A Mask is the persona she shows the prey. The Mask is the pretty lie, the identity that keeps her walking among the flock as an insider, even though she\u2019s nothing of the sort. It reflects how she deals with human society.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Dirge is who she is behind closed doors, and when dealing with other Kindred. A Dirge is the harsh truth to whichshe clings. It\u2019s the grounding point to which she always returns.<br /> When she walks the halls of Elysium, and works within her covenant, she presents her Dirge.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, the Mask is the human facade. The Dirge the vampiric existence. The Dirge is who you are in the dark with the other monsters aka your Kindred (vampires). The Mask is the lie you present to the human society.<br /> <br /> Willpower flows from strengthening or defending your Masks aka maintaining the Masquerade (that's what the Mask was called in Danse Macabre), and it flows from being a vampire when being a vampire to the exclusion of your humanity. Yes, it's a difficult act to balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T16:20:25-07:00","id":1154875,"title":"","content":"I agree with <b>Maina</b>. The actions would really be the same. But the reasons, and the context, do change.<br /> <br /> On a practical level, we can add the following to make things more clear:<br /> - Being your facade before the sheep, the Mask only gives you willpower when you have reason to think there can be mortals watching you.<br /> - Being your hidden self, the Dirge only gives you willpower when you have reason to think there can't be mortals watching you.<br /> <br /> The Mask wouldn't apply if you have no reason to think you're being watched, because it is about the facade, it isn't really important to you by itself. The Dirge wouldn't apply under the possibility of mortal scrutiny, because you would be too worried of being caught to reassure yourself. Vampires never affect this, because they're already predators for you. Even if you do keep a facade from them, it wouldn't be relevant for willpower gain.<br /> <br /> With that you can see how things play. The actions, again, are the same. But the situations where the character tries to act that way are opposite.<br /> <br /> And, of course, you can make both similar or the same, to represent someone who are truer to itself even as a monster. In that case, the same actions always reward willpower because they are true and the character isn't restrained from showing the true self.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T19:42:50-07:00","id":1154941,"title":"","content":"I would add that Mask and Dirge are not as simple as &quot;the fake persona&quot; and &quot;your true self&quot;. That's Nature and Demeanor. Mask and Dirge are a little more nuanced. Both are true aspects of yourself, but Mask is the aspect of yourself that you want others to perceive as defining you. That you want to believe defines you. Much like Virtue, it's the part of you that you like, that allows you to sleep through the day. Dirge is the part of you that you don't want other people to see. The dark desires that, shameful as they may be, make your Requiem worthwhile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T20:10:55-07:00","id":1154951,"title":"","content":"It gives me the feeling like there is another anchor missing.<br /> The Mask is how you present yourself to mortal, the fiction needed for you to survive among the mortals.<br /> The dirge would be how you present yourself to the kindred. I think it is a bad idea to show your true self to the rest of the all night society, but just the same you dont deal with other kindred the same way you deal with mortals.<br /> The way i see it you need a third one that represent who you really are. The part you dont show anyone. If we go that this is the dirge, then you'd need another mask for when interacting with kindred society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 11-01-2017, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T22:12:02-07:00","id":1154986,"title":"","content":"Dirge is who you really are.<br /> <br /> Mask has nothing to do with mortals; it's what you present to the world, both Kindred and Kine. It seems to be a recurring misunderstanding here, but Mask is not mortal-specific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T06:07:07-07:00","id":1155030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1154024-help-me-understand-mask-dirge?p=1154986#post1154986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dirge is who you really are.<br /> <br /> Mask has nothing to do with mortals; it's what you present to the world, both Kindred and Kine. It seems to be a recurring misunderstanding here, but Mask is not mortal-specific.</div> </div> </div> </div>At one point in the core we see this.<br /> ''Kindred wear Masks in public. A Mask is the persona she shows the prey. The Mask is the pretty lie, the identity that keeps her walking among the flock as an insider, even though she's nothing of the sort. <b>It reflect how she deals with human society</b>.<br /> The Dirge is who she is behind closed doors, <b>and when dealing with other kindred</b>. ... When she walks the halls of Elysium, and works within her covenant, she presents her Dirge '' pp. 80-81<br /> <br /> But, in agreement to what you said. We see later on in the book in the specific section of the anchors the relationship between the masks/humans and dirge/kindred, is much more ambivalent.<br /> With the mask being simply what you present to others (regardless of who these others are) and the Dirge being the ''truth behind the lies'' and ''the vampire's secret self''. p. 84<br /> <br /> So the book doesnt seem to decide exactly what Mask and Dirges are precisely or doesnt want to decide and prefers to let people pick however they prefer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T06:39:28-07:00","id":1155038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1154024-help-me-understand-mask-dirge?p=1154941#post1154941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would add that Mask and Dirge are not as simple as &quot;the fake persona&quot; and &quot;your true self&quot;. That's Nature and Demeanor. Mask and Dirge are a little more nuanced. Both are true aspects of yourself, but Mask is the aspect of yourself that you want others to perceive as defining you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I prefer this take as well. &quot;Secret desires or aspects of identity are truer&quot; has always struck me as simplistic. Two true selves, one of which you welcome others seeing, while the other you try to keep hidden, is much more interesting. So in the case of Authoritatian, you might do the same things, whichever of the two it is - but if it's your Mask, it will fulfill you to do them blatantly* and let others see your affinity for power - while if it's your Dirge, it'll fulfill you to be more circumspect about it and hide that part of yourself as much as you can.<br /> <br /> * At least to the extent that won't get you killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T06:59:45-07:00","id":1155041,"title":"","content":"In my reading, what Mask has to do with mortals is that it\u2019s the part of you that you use to pretend to be one. That is certainly something Kindred do among other Kindred - they may all recognize it\u2019s an act, but they keep it up anyway because they\u2019re a respectable society and that\u2019s what people in respectable societies do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T11:32:15-07:00","id":1155146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1154024-help-me-understand-mask-dirge?p=1155041#post1155041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my reading, what Mask has to do with mortals is that it\u2019s the part of you that you use to pretend to be one. That is certainly something Kindred do among other Kindred - they may all recognize it\u2019s an act, but they keep it up anyway because they\u2019re a respectable society and that\u2019s what people in respectable societies do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I go as well. Some Kindred (usually newer) use their Mask when interacting with other Kindred, while some Kindred (usually older) flout their Dirges in front of mortals all the time.<br /> <br /> My simplification for new players is: &quot;<i>Mask is how you act when prey are watching, Dirge is how you act when other predators are watching.</i>&quot; I don't see either as the pure truth/self - I leave that for the player's sense of the character's self. Rather, the 'pretty lie' of the Mask is the flip side of the 'chosen expression' of the Dirge.<br /> <br /> Who do you pretend to be, and who do you want to be? But who you <i>are</i> might not necessarily align with either of those answers.<br /> <br /> And this text bears repeating: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VtR2Ep84</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like Aspirations, anchors are not supernatural traits. They\u2019re a narrative mechanic that helps us portray Kindred psychology.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T12:00:39-07:00","id":1155155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1154024-help-me-understand-mask-dirge?p=1155146#post1155146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is how I go as well. Some Kindred (usually newer) use their Mask when interacting with other Kindred, while some Kindred (usually older) flout their Dirges in front of mortals all the time.<br /> <br /> My simplification for new players is: &quot;<i>Mask is how you act when prey are watching, Dirge is how you act when other predators are watching.</i>&quot; I don't see either as the pure truth/self - I leave that for the player's sense of the character's self. Rather, the 'pretty lie' of the Mask is the flip side of the 'chosen expression' of the Dirge.<br /> <br /> Who do you pretend to be, and who do you want to be? But who you <i>are</i> might not necessarily align with either of those answers.<br /> <br /> And this text bears repeating: </div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I tell people they were called Masquerade and Requiem through most of development and changed very shortly before the final release. Then I show them the section from the beginning of the book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are you going to do to make it through tonight? What about tomorrow night? And after the deeds are done and your belly\u2019s full, how are you going to live with yourself? What are you going to do with your damnation that makes it worth all the sins along the way?<br /> That\u2019s the Requiem.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s only half the question, though. Mortals are dinner, but they\u2019re also what you\u2019ve got for dates. No matter how callous you become, you\u2019ll need to move among them. How will you keep your connection to Humanity, even as a sham?<br /> That\u2019s the Masquerade. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T12:03:05-07:00","id":1155156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1154024-help-me-understand-mask-dirge?p=1155155#post1155155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I tell people they were called Masquerade and Requiem through most of development and changed very shortly before the final release. Then I show them the section from the beginning of the book:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T12:31:40-07:00","id":1155165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1154024-help-me-understand-mask-dirge?p=1155155#post1155155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I tell people they were called Masquerade and Requiem through most of development and changed very shortly before the final release. Then I show them the section from the beginning of the book:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Makes the most sense to me. Also aligns with p. 80-81. That's what I am using.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T19:38:27-07:00","id":1155257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1154024-help-me-understand-mask-dirge?p=1154875#post1154875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with <b>Maina</b>. The actions would really be the same. But the reasons, and the context, do change.<br /> <br /> On a practical level, we can add the following to make things more clear:<br /> - Being your facade before the sheep, the Mask only gives you willpower when you have reason to think there can be mortals watching you.<br /> - Being your hidden self, the Dirge only gives you willpower when you have reason to think there can't be mortals watching you.<br /> <br /> The Mask wouldn't apply if you have no reason to think you're being watched, because it is about the facade, it isn't really important to you by itself. The Dirge wouldn't apply under the possibility of mortal scrutiny, because you would be too worried of being caught to reassure yourself. Vampires never affect this, because they're already predators for you. Even if you do keep a facade from them, it wouldn't be relevant for willpower gain.<br /> <br /> With that you can see how things play. The actions, again, are the same. But the situations where the character tries to act that way are opposite.<br /> <br /> And, of course, you can make both similar or the same, to represent someone who are truer to itself even as a monster. In that case, the same actions always reward willpower because they are true and the character isn't restrained from showing the true self.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, now i get it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> So the important thing is what the action was meant to accomplish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T19:45:03-07:00","id":1155260,"title":"","content":"I don't feel comfortable reducing it in any way. Every interpretation is valid and makes for some good characters. That's why I like to go right for practical rules, so each person can interpret them as best suited for the character.<br /> <br /> But I still see nothing on the rules stating that you benefit from the Mask in front of other Vampires. That is why I like to treat them as &quot;for practical purposes on gaining willpower, Vampires don't matter&quot;. So it is ultimately up to you if you act in front of them as your Mask, your Dirge, or something else altogether. You can feel a lot of things toward your fellow Kindred, but their opinion on you isn't something emotionally reassuring for you to recover willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T19:50:29-07:00","id":1155262,"title":"","content":"I believe there's meant to be a higher frequency of spending and gaining Willpower in second edition, so there's no real reason to be stingy about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T19:57:55-07:00","id":1155264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1154024-help-me-understand-mask-dirge?p=1155260#post1155260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't feel comfortable reducing it in any way. Every interpretation is valid and makes for some good characters. That's why I like to go right for practical rules, so each person can interpret them as best suited for the character.<br /> <br /> But I still see nothing on the rules stating that you benefit from the Mask in front of other Vampires. That is why I like to treat them as &quot;for practical purposes on gaining willpower, Vampires don't matter&quot;. So it is ultimately up to you if you act in front of them as your Mask, your Dirge, or something else altogether. You can feel a lot of things toward your fellow Kindred, but their opinion on you isn't something emotionally reassuring for you to recover willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wouldn\u2019t be my interpretation, but if it works for you and Loki, that\u2019s all that matters.<br /> <br /> Me, I don\u2019t see anything rules-wise suggesting the Mask actions <i>wouldn\u2019t</i> grant Willpower when there are no humans around, nor Dirge when there are no vampires. If undeath is a ball, Mask is the clothes you wear to the party and Dirge is the song you dance to. You don\u2019t take your tux off just because you think your crush isn\u2019t looking at you, and when your favorite song comes on you dance like no one is watching, even if they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}